            "contentType": "VIDEO",
            "title": "Rare earth stocks surge, Broadcom pops on OpenAI deal",
            "description": "<p>Here are some of the stories Wall Street is watching on Monday, Oct. 13. OpenAI (<a data-i13n=\"cpos:1;pos:1\" href=\"https://finance.yahoo.com/quote/OPAI.PVT\">OPAI.PVT</a>) and Broadcom (<a data-i13n=\"cpos:2;pos:1\" href=\"https://finance.yahoo.com/quote/AVGO\">AVGO</a>) <a data-i13n=\"cpos:3;pos:1\" href=\"https://finance.yahoo.com/news/openai-and-broadcom-sign-deal-to-build-up-to-10-gigawatts-of-custom-chips-broadcom-stock-surges-135932920.html\">announced an agreement</a> for data center chips. Rare earth stocks are surging on continued tensions between the US and China. Jefferies Financial (<a data-i13n=\"cpos:4;pos:1\" href=\"https://finance.yahoo.com/quote/JEF\">JEF</a>) is seeking to reassure investors following the bankruptcy of auto-parts supplier First Brands.</p>\n<p>Stay up to date on the latest market action, minute-by-minute, with <a data-i13n=\"cpos:5;pos:1\" href=\"https://finance.yahoo.com/videos/series/market-minute/\">Yahoo Finance's Market Minute.</a></p>",
